From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 03:50:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] feat(ui): a reviewer's layout: one dock at the bottom,
 layers folded, the Hand first

On this instance people look, comment and review; the agents design. With
FULL_UI off (as 0005 has it), on a desktop with floating panels, the
editor's chrome moves out of the canvas's way:

- No top bar, no tool rail, no side rail. One dock along the bottom
  (CanvasDock.tsx), icons only with their names on hover: back to the
  canvases, the canvas's name and its id (# opens copy id / copy link);
  Hand, Comment and Prototype mode, the tool picked from the list, and the
  rest of the tools in a list that opens upwards; the zoom (the Stage
  draws its own control into the dock, menu and handlers included); who is
  here; Import and Export; Comments and AI activity, which open the
  right-hand panel on that tab and close it again, and Connect AI; the
  design panel, settings and you.
- Present stays at the top right, beside the open panels.
- The Hand is the first tool; the right-hand panel starts closed; the
  right-hand panels end above the dock.
- Layers folds under the pages and starts folded (doop:layers-section).
- Phones and the docked panel layout keep their own chrome, and
  localStorage['doop:full-ui'] = 'on' brings the whole old layout back.

Shown first as before / after frames on a doop canvas and changed as
asked.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
